    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Abraham Lincoln helped plat the town and served as counsel for the Chicago & Mississippi Railroad before the town was named after him.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincoln%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area’s history dates back to the 1850s and 1860s when farmers turned prairie into farmland that later became Lincoln Square.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lincolnsquare.org/cultural-information"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lincoln Square’s streets are lined with murals and public art that invite residents to stroll and experience the neighborhood’s rich cultural tapestry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
